  "title": "India's Starlink Policy and Elon Musk's Remarks",
  "summary": "Nishikant Dubey, the chair of the Standing Committee on IT, argues that India's security policy is not shaped by social media pressure and counters Elon Musk's criticism of Starlink's entry into India. Musk claims Starlink must offer affordable services in India, while his allegations against Reliance India face criticism from BJP MP Nishikant Dubey and former NITI Aayog vice-chairman Rajiv Kumar.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Elon Musk claims Starlink must offer affordable services in India to compete with local telecom providers.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Musk argues that competition will benefit consumers in India and that Ambani's profits will be lower, but he does not abandon his position.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Musk's remarks come as Jio Platforms, the digital arm of Reliance Industries, prepares for India's biggest public offering.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
